    "Label choice for ATmega pins: the AVR port names (PB5, PC0...) were treated as port names, not GPIO names, so the Arduino names (D13, A0/D14) were used as labels.",
    "ISP header is drawn as a detached diagram, so 'row nearest the board edge' is undefined; top row chosen as the outer row. A bar mark above the MISO pin may indicate pin 1 but is not labeled."
  ],
  "notes": "SparkFun RedBoard (DEV-13975) pinout. White 'Name' boxes are the silkscreen and are placed first in functions when they differ; the Arduino name (D13, A0/D14) is used as the label. Lower digital pin 7 shows 'IN1' as printed. A bar is drawn above the top-right ISP pin (MISO) but no '1' is printed."
